================================================================================
TEARDOWN
================================================================================
Run WITHOUT `--stop-on-error`, deliberately. While a mirror is configured, entering the
destination port's interface mode prints a `% ` line that is an ADVISORY, not a rejection -- the
command succeeds and the prompt advances. A stop-on-error heuristic reads it as a failure and
aborts the sequence before the `no mirror interface` ever runs. The teardown is therefore gated
on PROVEN STATE instead of on an exit code.

  x960-56YSQ#configure terminal
  Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
  x960-56YSQ(config)#interface port1.0.11
  % port1.0.11 is currently configured as a mirror-port. Use caution when altering its config
  x960-56YSQ(config-if)#no mirror interface port1.0.10
  x960-56YSQ(config-if)#end
  x960-56YSQ#show mirror
  x960-56YSQ#show running-config interface port1.0.11
  !
  interface port1.0.11
   switchport
   switchport mode access
  !

(17:14:02 - 17:14:08 NZDT)

  - `show mirror` prints NOTHING          -> the mirror is gone
  - port1.0.11 is back to `switchport` / `switchport mode access` with no mirror line

The `no` form was given its argument (`port1.0.10`) because a bare `no mirror interface` is
`% Incomplete command` on this platform -- `no mirror interface ?` offers IFRANGE and none and
has no `<cr>`.

